by javiereguiluz at 2026-07-27T15:41:55Z

@stof you are right that context in PO files is namespacing, not just normal metadata.

However, including context is apparently common in many tools used to generate PO files. So, changing the bahvior to throw excepctions when any context is present could be too harsh.

I propose this instead:

* Keep storing (and reloading) the context inside metadata to not lose that information
* Throw only if two different messages have the same key but different contexts. Nowadays, the later occurrence silently overwrites the first one

